# Cloudflare Pages response headers (copied to dist/ by Vite).
# Cross-origin isolation lets the AI assistant (wllama) use several CPU threads,
# which Firefox needs: its WebGPU is too slow for the models. DuckDB keeps its
# single-threaded bundle: the jsDelivr manifest has no threaded one.
# Every cross-origin resource must send CORS or Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy
# headers (jsDelivr, extensions.duckdb.org, and Hugging Face do).
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
